From: Valerie Snyder <valsnyde@cisco.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:24:21 -0400
Subject: libclammspack: Bound CHM directory traversal (#152)

CHM directory lookup follows archive-controlled PMGI and PMGL chunk
references. Cyclic references can cause chmd_fast_find() to loop
indefinitely.

Limit each traversal to the number of declared directory chunks and
reject out-of-range child indexes, returning the existing data-format
error for malformed archives.

Reported by Nebula Security.

CLAM-3069

---
Upstream: https://github.com/Cisco-Talos/clamav/commit/f2d309f55f6581718350cfd86cfeed5e3ac8970c
CVE: CVE-2026-76414
Signed-off-by: Titouan Christophe <titouan.christophe@mind.be>
---
 libclammspack/mspack/chmd.c | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libclammspack/mspack/chmd.c b/libclammspack/mspack/chmd.c
index 27cbed67fa..0d5c3d5c42 100644
